ry i, diam A_i≤ρ_i≤δ, B_i⊆J_i, and J_i is either empty or an open interval of length at most ρ_i+η_i; η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s)>0.", "binders": [], "objects": ["A_i", "B_i", "J", "ρ", "δ", "η", "ε", "s"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": ["L2"], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S003", "text": "For any t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E: for any x∈E some V_i contains (x,t), and then x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. By F002 this is a δ-cover, whose s-cost is at most Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Hence c≤Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t) for every t∈I. Define f_i(t)=ρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Every f_i is nonnegative and Borel measurable because J_i is open and its coefficient is a fixed finite nonnegative real. In particular it is almost-everywhere measurable for Lebesgue measure restricted to I.", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F001", "F002"], "objects": ["c", "E", "I", "F", "V", "A_i", "B_i", "J", "ρ", "s", "δ", "f"], "produces": [{"id": "F003", "statement": "For every t∈I, c≤Σ_i f_i(t), where f_i(t)=ρ_i^s1_{J_i}(t); each f_i is Borel measurable and hence Lebesgue-almost-everywhere measurable for the restricted measure on I.", "binders": [{"symbol": "t", "type": "real number in I"}], "objects": ["t", "I", "c", "f", "ρ", "s", "J"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": [], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S004", "text": "Integrate F003 against Lebesgue measure restricted to I. Its total mass is one by M007 with endpoints 0,1. Monotonicity of the nonnegative integral, the integral of a constant, and M005 applied to the nonnegative measurable series yield c≤Σ_i∫_I f_i(t)dt=Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|. Here the integral of a constant times a measurable indicator is that constant times its set's measure, directly the simple-function integral formula. By M008 and monotonicity of measure, |J_i∩I|≤|J_i|≤ρ_i+η_i (the empty case is zero). Consequently c≤Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+Σ_iη_iρ_i^s≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε, because η_iρ_i^s=ε2^{-i-1}ρ_i^s/(1+ρ_i^s)≤ε2^{-i-1} and Σ_{i≥0}2^{-i-1}=1. All series are nonnegative; their order comparisons and splitting are valid also when a sum is infinite.", "uses": ["M005", "M007", "M008"], "uses_local": ["F001", "F002", "F003"], "objects": ["c", "I", "f", "J", "ρ", "η", "s", "ε"], "produces": [{"id": "F004", "statement": "c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε for the arbitrary δ-cover V and arbitrary ε>0.", "binders": [], "objects": ["c", "ρ", "s", "ε", "V", "δ"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": [], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S005", "text": "If Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}=∞, the desired bound c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1} is immediate. If the sum is finite, F004 for all ε>0 gives that bound by letting ε↓0. Since V was any δ-cover of F, taking the infimum of its (s+1)-costs gives Hscale(s,δ,E)=c≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F). The construction of J depended on ε, but c and this cover's cost did not, so the limit is legitimate. Discharge the arbitrary-cover restrictions and s>0,δ>0,ε>0 restrictions and universally quantify s,δ. This proves the slicing inequality.", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F001", "F004"], "objects": ["V", "ρ", "s", "δ", "ε", "c", "E", "F", "J", "Hscale"], "produces": [], "introduces": [], "discharges": ["L2", "L1"]}], "applications": [{"input": "M005", "at": "S004", "bindings": "Set α=ℝ with its Borel measurable structure, μ=Lebesgue measure restricted to I, β=ℕ and use f_i from S003.", "hypothesis_checks": ["Lebesgue measure restricted to the Borel set I is a measure on this measurable space.", "The series index is ℕ, a countable type.", "F003 proves Borel measurability of every f_i, hence almost-everywhere measurability for μ."]}, {"input": "M007", "at": "S004", "bindings": "Set a=0 and b=1; the interval [a,b] is I.", "hypothesis_checks": []}, {"input": "M008", "at": "S004", "bindings": "For each nonempty V_i set a=inf B_i-η_i/2 and b=sup B_i+η_i/2, so (a,b)=J_i; empty members contribute zero separately.", "hypothesis_checks": []}]}, "warning": "Direct inputs and fixed logic are supplied. Audit A may record positively checked routine background under the declared policy, with logged pinned-lib